<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alpujarras</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Las Alpujarras</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Alpujarras is a mountainous region on the southern slopes of the Sierra <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a> in the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Under the Nasrids it was a densely settled land of terraced, irrigated farms and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> production. It was the centre of two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> revolts, in 1499–1501 and 1568–1571, after which its Morisco population was deported and replaced by settlers from northern Spain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alpujarras.jpg" alt="Alpujarras" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Alpujarra.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
